WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.646
Scheduling offers a time only when it is really free.

00:00:04.646 --> 00:00:07.922
This video shows how open times are worked out:

00:00:07.922 --> 00:00:12.371
working hours and days off, busy time on a calendar, the free time

00:00:12.371 --> 00:00:15.461
around appointments, and the booking limits.

00:00:15.461 --> 00:00:18.860
It also shows what to check when no times appear.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:29.453
A time is offered when the whole appointment fits inside the working hours of the resource.

00:00:29.453 --> 00:00:34.520
With All resources together, it must fit inside the hours of every resource.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:39.469
It must also be clear of anything busy on the resource's calendar, and

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:42.176
for a staff member, on their own calendars.

00:00:42.176 --> 00:00:46.099
The free time before and after the appointment has to be clear as

00:00:46.099 --> 00:00:50.630
well, and so does the free time around appointments that are already booked.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.897
Finally, the booking limits apply:

00:00:53.897 --> 00:00:59.247
the minimum notice, how far ahead customers can book, the most appointments per

00:00:59.247 --> 00:01:01.890
day, and the places left in a class.

00:01:06.094 --> 00:01:10.115
Open Calendars, Appointments and choose Book an appointment.

00:01:10.115 --> 00:01:14.564
Pick Initial consultation, choose a Tuesday, and choose Show times.

00:01:15.014 --> 00:01:15.546
Dr.

00:01:15.546 --> 00:01:19.443
Maya Chen works from nine to twelve and from one to five, so

00:01:19.443 --> 00:01:22.100
the times fall inside those two ranges.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.824
The lunch break has none, and the times step by the value set on the type.

00:01:27.277 --> 00:01:31.484
The appointment itself has to fit inside the hours, but its free time

00:01:31.484 --> 00:01:34.400
after only has to be clear of other busy time.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.597
So the last time of a range can run into the break.

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:39.291
Now a day off.

00:01:39.291 --> 00:01:43.760
December 24th is listed as closed on her resource, so there are no

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.249
open times at all.

00:01:45.702 --> 00:01:50.811
Physiotherapy takes Omar Hassan and Treatment room 1 together, so a time is

00:01:50.811 --> 00:01:53.208
offered only when both are free.

00:01:53.208 --> 00:01:56.552
Omar works on Mondays, so a Monday shows times.

00:01:57.004 --> 00:02:01.518
On a Tuesday he doesn't work, and with All resources together nothing is

00:02:01.518 --> 00:02:04.064
offered, even though the room is free.

00:02:08.257 --> 00:02:12.267
Anything busy on a resource's calendar closes its times.

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:15.629
Open Calendar, choose New event, and under Dr.

00:02:15.629 --> 00:02:17.957
Maya Chen choose Blocked time.

00:02:18.408 --> 00:02:21.796
Give it a title, such as Staff meeting, and set it from two

00:02:21.796 --> 00:02:24.768
to three in the afternoon on Tuesday, then save it.

00:02:26.089 --> 00:02:30.639
Back on the booking page, the times from one thirty to two thirty are gone.

00:02:30.639 --> 00:02:34.684
The one thirty visit would end at two o'clock, but its ten minutes

00:02:34.684 --> 00:02:37.269
of free time would run into the meeting.

00:02:37.721 --> 00:02:39.189
Now book a visit.

00:02:39.189 --> 00:02:44.681
Choose ten o'clock, enter the customer's name, email and phone, and choose Book.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.708
A booked appointment keeps its free time clear too.

00:02:49.708 --> 00:02:54.004
Back on the same day, nine thirty, ten and ten thirty are gone.

00:02:54.004 --> 00:02:57.490
Nine o'clock and eleven o'clock are still offered.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:05.253
The booking rules of the appointment type add limits.

00:03:05.253 --> 00:03:09.480
Open Calendars, Appointment Types and edit Initial consultation.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:12.680
Minimum notice hides times that start too soon.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:16.621
Book up to hides times that are too far ahead, and Most per

00:03:16.621 --> 00:03:20.699
resource per day stops one resource taking more than that many of this

00:03:20.699 --> 00:03:21.773
type in a day.

00:03:22.224 --> 00:03:24.036
A class works differently.

00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:27.999
The Yoga class has eight places, so each of its times stays open

00:03:27.999 --> 00:03:30.604
until the eighth customer has booked it.

00:03:34.804 --> 00:03:38.367
If a day shows no times, check the appointment type first.

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:42.932
It needs Resources, and each of them must have Takes appointments ticked and

00:03:42.932 --> 00:03:45.104
working hours that cover the day.

00:03:45.854 --> 00:03:48.696
Then check the limits, and anything busy:

00:03:48.696 --> 00:03:53.111
a blocked time or event on the resource's calendar, or on the staff

00:03:53.111 --> 00:03:56.074
member's own calendars, closes those times.

00:03:58.074 --> 00:04:02.592
A time is offered only when the hours, the calendars, the free time

00:04:02.592 --> 00:04:07.605
and the limits all agree, so the same person or room is never booked twice.

00:04:07.605 --> 00:04:09.214
Thanks for watching.

